{"white":"NikoTheodorou","black":"Sina-Movahed","whiteElo":"3238","blackElo":"3302","result":"1-0","opening":"King's Indian Defense: Orthodox Variation","as":"w","accuracy":{"w":91.7,"b":88.8},"counts":{"w":{"best":16,"brilliant":1},"b":{"best":14,"great":1,"blunder":1}},"moment":{"name":"36.Bd3","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","fen":"q2r3k/p4pb1/1pn4p/5Qp1/3B4/1P1B4/P5PP/3R3K b - - 5 36","from":"e2","to":"d3"},"finalFen":"q2r3k/p4pb1/1pn4p/5Qp1/3B4/1P1B4/P5PP/3R3K b - - 5 36"},"white":"NikoTheodorou","black":"Sina-Movahed","labels":["book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","best","good","best","best","excellent","best","best","inaccuracy","best","best","best","best","good","best","best","best","excellent","best","good","best","best","good","best","best","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","good","good","best","best","best","best","good","inaccuracy","good","best","best","good","excellent","excellent","best","best","great","excellent","blunder","brilliant"],"moments":[{"ply":68,"name":"34…Qa8","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"34…Qa8! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moving away uncovers the rook on d8, which now hits the rook on d1.","Moves the attacked queen to safety.","The next best move, 34…Qxd1, would drop Black's winning chances from 49% to 13% (+5.27).","34…Qa8 gets the queen out of the way of Rxd5.","White was threatening Rxd5, winning the queen for a rook. The queen steps away.","White answers 35.a4."]},{"ply":70,"name":"35…Nc6","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"35…Nc6 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 51% to 0%.","points":["White answers 36.Bd3.","Better was 35…Qc8 (−0.16)."],"better":"35…Qc8 threatens …Qxf5, winning the queen, and stops Bxe5. After 36.Qxc8 Rxc8 37.Bxe5 Bxe5 38.Bc4 Rc7, the queens come off (−0.16)."},{"ply":71,"name":"36.Bd3","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","headline":"36.Bd3!! A real sacrifice: White gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Leaves the bishop on d4 where it can be taken.","Taking is too dangerous: Black's best reply is 36…Kg8 37.Qh7+ Kf8 38.Qxg7+ instead (the engine rates it +30.65).","36.Bd3 threatens Qh7#, with mate in 1, and stops …Nxd4.","It threatens Qh7#, with mate in 1, so Black has to spend the next move on it.","Black was threatening …Nxd4, winning a rook for a pawn. Bd3 takes care of it.","The engine's plan continues with Qh7+ and Qxg7+: this move is the first step."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"36.Bd3!! leaves the bishop on d4 hanging. Taking it leads to mate."},{"title":"What White gives up","text":"The bishop on d4 is attacked by the knight on c6, the bishop on g7 and the rook on d8, and 36.Bd3 doesn't save it. That's a bishop on offer."},{"title":"What it does instead","text":"It threatens Qh7# and mate."},{"title":"If Black takes the bishop","text":"36…Rxd4 is met by 37.Qh7#, and it's mate."},{"title":"Black's best try","text":"Black's best is to leave the bishop alone and play 36…Kg8. White answers 37.Qh7+. Then 38.Qxg7+ gives check, and 39.Qf6+ gives check. White ends up a piece and a pawn ahead: White is winning (+30.65)."},{"title":"Why not save the bishop first?","text":"Saving it with 36.Bxg7+, the best way to do that, is clearly weaker (+4.25 against +30.65). Black answers 36…Kxg7, taking the bishop on g7 and threatening …Rxd1+, with a dangerous check. White would still be winning, but far less than after 36.Bd3."}]}],"opening":{"name":"King's Indian Defense: Orthodox Variation","eco":"E94","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 11.Nc2: 21 moves in all, 11 by White and 10 by Black.","Theory runs out after 11.Nc2: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}